# Line endings are LF, in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# This is not a preference. `core.autocrlf` is true on the machine this project
# is developed on, and the folder here is the extension itself, loaded unpacked
# from this very path. Without this file the first checkout rewrites all 116
# files to CRLF in the live code, which shows up as a diff on everything while
# changing nothing, and the project's own rule is to preserve line endings
# because a careless rewrite has already corrupted the feed's button glyphs once.
#
# Declaring it here settles it for every clone instead of depending on a global
# setting nobody else has.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pictures and archives are never converted. The screenshots in the README and
# the extension's icons are the ones that would be destroyed by it.
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.zip -text
*.mp4 -text

# A PowerShell script is read by Windows tooling, which is content with LF, and
# a mixed rule here would be one more thing to keep in step.
